  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "b8379957-67f0-44c3-b1ad-47a5c8803af4",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        560,
        96
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Parent Incident/Complaint Report  - Slack Notify\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow collects a parent incident or complaint report from a form, creates a ticket, and looks up student details in Google Sheets. Based on the lookup result, it either continues to validate attachments and classify the complaint with Gemini, or follows an alternate path to retrieve student details and send a WhatsApp message. Classified reports are appended or updated in Google Sheets, formatted for Slack, posted to a Slack channel, and followed by a confirmation form response.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the form trigger fields for parent contact details, student ID, incident details, and any attachment upload expected by the workflow.\n- Connect Google Sheets credentials and select the correct spreadsheets/ranges for both student lookup nodes and the complaint log node.\n- Configure Google Gemini credentials for the multimodal complaint classification chain and ensure the structured output parser matches the fields expected by the sheet and Slack message.\n- Connect Slack credentials and set the destination channel or user for incident notifications.\n- Connect WhatsApp credentials and verify the recipient/phone-number mapping used in the alternate branch.\n\n### Customization\n\nYou can customize the ticket fields, Gemini classification schema, Google Sheets columns, Slack message template, and WhatsApp notification content to match the school\u2019s incident reporting process."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "7cbd602f-f854-45d3-a834-77010e0b4d82",
